 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`Kinematics/Basic.lean:151-174` holds the new `namespace Witness`; its header says the file \"introduces the abstract bilinear form `Bilin` ... and a minimal kinematic record\" (`:15-17`). `gWit` uses only `Bilin`, i.e. `LinearMap.BilinForm \u211d (\u211d \u00d7 \u211d \u00d7 \u211d)` (`:41`), and nothing from `DisKinematics`. The repo already separates such material into its own modules: `QFT/Jets/Observable/Counterexamples.lean` and this PR's `QFT/Jets/Frame/Witness.lean`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Kinematics/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Put the shared form in its own module and import it from the three consumers (`Tensors/Basic.lean`, `Polarized/Kinematics.lean`, `Jets/Frame/Witness.lean`): either `EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Kinematics/Witness.lean`, or \u2014 since it is just a Minkowski bilinear form \u2014 a generic module beside the rest of the form API under `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/BilinearForm/`.",
   "issue": "`Witness.gWit`/`gWit_apply`/`gWit_isSymm` are moved into the abstract DIS foundation file, which the module docstring describes as the `Bilin` abbreviation plus a \"minimal kinematic record\". The `+--` form on `\u211d \u00d7 \u211d \u00d7 \u211d` carries no DIS content, witnesses nothing declared in this file, and is now in the import closure of every DIS module and of `QFT/Jets` (via `Frame/Basic.lean`); `@[simp] gWit_apply`, a lemma about one concrete three-dimensional example, is exported to all of them. The PR itself puts the jets witness in its own module (`Jets/Frame/Witness.lean`), so the two witnesses are placed inconsistently.",
   "line": 151
  }
 ],
